<Project xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003">
  <!--
    DTIControls.targets — native dependency flow for the Lib-drop distribution model.

    Microsoft.Data.SqlClient's SNI libraries (Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.SNI.x64/x86.dll) are
    NATIVE. They are not listed in any managed assembly's reference table, so MSBuild's
    reference resolver cannot see them — a plain reference to DTIControls.dll (or to
    Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.dll) will copy the MANAGED closure to a dependent's bin but will
    NEVER copy these natives. Without them, connection.Open() fails at runtime on .NET Framework.

    This file lives in the Lib folder next to the DLLs. Import it ONCE per dependent project
    (or once in a repo-root Directory.Build.targets to cover every project automatically):

        <Import Project="..\Lib\DTIControls.targets" />

    Adjust the relative path to wherever Lib sits relative to the project. After that single
    edit the flow is transparent: drop refreshed DLLs/SNI into Lib and every dependent picks
    them up on its next build — no project changes, no version bumps. The wildcard means new
    or updated SNI files are picked up automatically.

    The managed assemblies (Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.dll, Azure.*, Microsoft.Identity*, etc.)
    flow on their own via the DLL reference graph as long as they sit in Lib — only the
    natives need to be handled here.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.SNI.*.dll">
      <Link>%(Filename)%(Extension)</Link>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Visible>false</Visible>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
